{
    // ============================================================
    // LiteBox VS Code Remote Server demo workspace
    // ============================================================
    //
    // Open this folder in VS Code from a WSL bash shell in ANY
    // litebox worktree (tasks are anchored at
    // `${workspaceFolder}/../..`, which resolves to the repo root
    // of whichever worktree you opened the demo from — main, or
    // any sibling work-stream worktree):
    //
    //   cd <worktree>/litebox_tool_executor/demo-vscode-server
    //   code .
    //
    // Then run the one-shot task:
    //
    //   Terminal → Run Task → "LiteBox: Setup and Start VS Code Server"
    //
    // which runs three tasks in sequence:
    //
    //   1. "LiteBox: Build"                — cargo build the litebox binaries.
    //   2. "LiteBox: Build VS Code Image"  — docker build litebox-vscode.
    //   3. "LiteBox: Start VS Code Server" — docker run the image with --vscode-server.
    //
    // The three are also runnable individually if you only need to
    // redo one step.
    //
    // Then in a separate VS Code window, Remote-SSH connect to
    // `litebox` (configure `~/.ssh/config` Host litebox HostName
    // 127.0.0.1 Port 2222 User root + empty password — dropbear
    // is started with `-B` to allow blank-password root login for
    // this demo).
    //
    // Recommended VS Code profile setup for Remote-SSH against
    // litebox (one-time, application-scoped settings — put them
    // in your "LiteBox" profile's user settings.json, not here):
    //
    //   "remote.SSH.showLoginTerminal": true,
    //   "remote.SSH.remotePlatform": { "litebox": "linux" }
    //
    // (Don't add `remote.SSH.enableReconnection: false` — it's
    // deprecated and ignored by current Remote-SSH; VS Code shows
    // it as grayed-out unknown. The "fail fast when the demo
    // container stops" behavior is bounded by the
    // ConnectionAttempts 1 + ServerAliveCountMax 1 in the
    // ~/.ssh/config block below, which clamps the underlying ssh
    // client's reconnect window.)
    //
    // And in ~/.ssh/config:
    //
    //   Host litebox
    //     HostName 127.0.0.1
    //     Port 2222
    //     User root
    //     PreferredAuthentications password
    //     PubkeyAuthentication no
    //     NumberOfPasswordPrompts 1
    //     StrictHostKeyChecking no
    //     UserKnownHostsFile /dev/null  ; on Windows: NUL
    //     ConnectionAttempts 1
    //     ServerAliveCountMax 1
    //
    // (On Windows + WSL2, the file Remote-SSH actually reads is
    // %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\config — VS Code on Windows uses Windows
    // OpenSSH, not WSL's ssh. UserKnownHostsFile must be `NUL`
    // there, not `/dev/null`.)
    //
    // ============================================================
    // For repeatable automated validation (no human in the loop)
    // use the integration test suite instead — see
    // `litebox_test_harness/tests/integration.rs` mod vscode:
    //
    //   cargo test -p litebox_test_harness --test integration -- 'vscode::'
    //
    // (or use the "LiteBox: Run Integration Tests (vscode::*)"
    //  task in this workspace.)
    // ============================================================

    // No workspace-scoped overrides today. All knobs live in the
    // user-profile settings above (per Remote-SSH application
    // scope) or in tasks.json.
}
